ef 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517655 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067792 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517711 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067792 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517835 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067792 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067792 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067792 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186517525 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067792 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ab495d5c-1e27-5baa-8e34-728ab73fbe3f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068026 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186068030 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068026 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517536 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068026 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517692 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068026 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517840 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068026 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517933 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068026 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068026 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068026 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186517692 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068026 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fb97819c-0e4a-5ac6-a889-9c7ec737b994" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068030 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{6}{5}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068030 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068030 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "13f74ec9-b3e2-592c-9d7d-428e27523b8c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068559 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4027" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068559 #edb/ref 1071 "What are the solutions to $x^2 + 16 = 0?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068559 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d659780a-f726-5827-a13a-a64b21a0cf41" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068559 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\tx^2 + 16 &= 0 \\[3pt]\n\t\tx^2 &= -16\n}\n$$\n\nBy taking the square root, we obtain\n\n$$\nx = \\pm \\sqrt{-16}.\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $x$ using the imaginary unit $\\textrm{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\, \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\pm \\sqrt{-16} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{16\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{16}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm 4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x = \\pm 4 \\textrm{i}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068560 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4028" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068560 #edb/ref 1071 "If $p^2 + 27 = 0,$ then $p =$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068560 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8082e3bd-04dc-5598-93c5-dbc423cdba97" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068560 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\np^2 + 27 & = 0\\[3pt]\n\np^2 & = -27 \n}\n$$\n\nBy taking the square root, we obtain\n\n$$\np = \\pm \\sqrt{-27}.\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $p$ using the imaginary unit $\\textrm{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\, \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =\\pm \\sqrt{-27} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{27\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{27}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{{3}^{2}\\cdot 3}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm 3\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm 3\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $p = \\pm 3\\sqrt{3} \\, \\textrm{i}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068561 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4029" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068561 #edb/ref 1071 "If $16z^2 + 49 = 0,$ then $z =$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068561 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "99f522f8-39ff-5612-86d1-84e703bde35f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068561 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n16z^2 + 49 & = 0\\[5pt]\n\n16z^2 & = -49 \\[5pt]\n\nz^2 & = -\\dfrac{49}{16}\n}\n$$\n\nBy taking the square root, we obtain\n\n$$\nz = \\pm \\sqrt{-\\dfrac{49}{16}}.\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $z$ using the imaginary unit $\\textrm{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\, \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{49}{16}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{49}{16}\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{49}{16}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{49}}{\\sqrt{16}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{7}{4}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $z=\\pm \\dfrac{7}{4} \\textrm{i}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068562 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4030" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068562 #edb/ref 1071 "What are the solutions of the equation $2y^2 + 9 = 0?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068562 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "93aec687-49af-55ea-9212-b33dd29f4ce7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068562 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t2y^2 + 9 &= 0 \\[5pt]\n\n\t\t2y^2 &= -9\\[5pt]\n\ny^2 & = -\\dfrac{9}{2}\n}\n$$\n\nBy taking square root, we obtain\n\n$$\ny = \\pm \\sqrt{-\\dfrac{9}{2}}.\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $y$ using the imaginary unit $\\textrm{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\, \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{9}{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{9}{2}\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{9}{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{9}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rationalize the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}\\text{i} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $y=\\pm \\dfrac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\textrm{i}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068705 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048187 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068705 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048428 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068705 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069306 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068705 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069308 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068705 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186234012 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068705 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186234013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068705 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/re