437 #edb/ref 1071 "What are the solutions of the equation $8{y}^{2}+12=0?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069437 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "47b94063-7f34-5826-9273-858fa9727be7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069437 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{y}^{2}+12 & =0 \\\\ 8{y}^{2} & =-12 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-\\frac{12}{8} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy taking square root, we obtain:\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{3}{2}}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $y$ using the imaginary unit $\\text{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{3}{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rationalize the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\text{i} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069476 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186068026 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069476 #edb/ref 1069 "q-66254" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069476 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069476 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the solutions of the equation $25{z}^{2}+36=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069476 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0e3bf3f1-d937-55da-b28c-d65551dd4623" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069476 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25{z}^{2}+36 & =0 \\\\ 25{z}^{2} & =-36 \\\\ {z}^{2} & =-\\frac{36}{25}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy taking square root, we obtain:\n\n$$\nz=\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{36}{25}}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $z$ using the imaginary unit $\\text{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{36}{25}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\s