qrt{-1}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{25}{64}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{25}{64}\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{25}{64}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{25}}{\\sqrt{64}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{5}{8}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518133 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186518082 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518133 #edb/ref 1069 "q-113227" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518133 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518133 #edb/ref 1071 "What are the solutions of the equation $27{y}^{2}+63=0?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518133 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4f3f1aa3-5d05-5a94-a6c1-299187fd64c9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518133 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}27{y}^{2}+63 & =0 \\\\ 27{y}^{2} & =-63 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-\\frac{63}{27} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-\\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy taking square root, we obtain:\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{7}{3}}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $y$ using the imaginary unit $\\text{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{7}{3}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{7}{3}\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{7}{3}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{3}}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rationalize the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{3}}\\text{i} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{3}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518139 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186517970 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518139 #edb/ref 1069 "q-3798" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518139 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518139 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine the solutions of the equation ${f}^{2}=-25.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518139 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "54e8fcf4-d538-5483-805d-02e6f387fbe1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518139 #edb/ref 1074 "By taking square root, we obtain:\n\n$$\nf=\\pm \\sqrt{-25}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $f$ using the imaginary unit $\\text{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f & =\\pm \\sqrt{-25} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{25\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{25}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm 5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518151 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186517999 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518151 #edb/ref 1069 "q-3800" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518151 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518151 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the solutions of $-2{d}^{2}-32=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518151 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6745c884-99da-504f-8dea-4d79761c7ad9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518151 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{d}^{2}-32 & =0 \\\\ -2{d}^{2} & =32 \\\\ {d}^{2} & =-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy taking square root, we obtain:\n\n$$\nd=\\pm \\sqrt{-16}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $d$ using the imaginary unit $\\text{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\pm \\sqrt{-16} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{16\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{16}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm 4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518159 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186518036 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518159 #edb/ref 1069 "q-112361" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518159 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518159 #edb/ref 1071 "If $\\frac{{w}^{2}}{4}+22=0,$ then $w=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518159 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "77b8b796-0079-55bf-a33c-a1e9a651dc45" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518159 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{w}^{2}}{4}+22 & =0 \\\\ \\frac{{w}^{2}}{4} & =-22 \\\\ {w}^{2} & =-88\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy taking square root, we obtain:\n\n$$\nw=\\pm \\sqrt{-88}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $w$ using the imaginary unit $\\text{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w & =\\pm \\sqrt{-88} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{88\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{88}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm 2\\sqrt{22}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm 2\\sqrt{22}\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518197 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186517969 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518197 #edb/ref 1069 "q-66250" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518197 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518197 #edb/ref 1071 "If ${y}^{2}+63=0,$ then $y=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518197 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cd11ce23-27fe-5c7c-9502-a02ca58513ca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518197 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}+63 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-63\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy taking square root, we obtain:\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\sqrt{-63}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $y$ using the imaginary unit $\\text{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\sqrt{-63} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{63\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{63}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm 3\\sqrt{7}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm 3\\sqrt{7}\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
